<item>
            <title>[LU-20570] auster results.yml is invalid YAML when a failure message contains an apostrophe</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20570</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;tt&gt;yml_log_sub_test_end()&lt;/tt&gt; in &lt;tt&gt;lustre/tests/yaml.sh&lt;/tt&gt; writes a subtest&apos;s failure message into &lt;tt&gt;results.yml&lt;/tt&gt; with shell quoting placed inside a YAML double-quoted scalar:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;preformatted panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;preformattedContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;printf &apos;            error: &quot;%q&quot;\n&apos; &quot;$*&quot;
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;tt&gt;%q&lt;/tt&gt; quotes for &lt;b&gt;bash&lt;/b&gt;; the surrounding &lt;tt&gt;&quot;...&quot;&lt;/tt&gt; is a &lt;b&gt;YAML&lt;/b&gt; double-quoted scalar, where the only legal escapes are the ones YAML defines. The two disagree, so a failure message can either break the file or be recorded wrong.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;&lt;a name=&quot;Symptom1%3Athefilewillnotparse&quot;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Symptom 1: the file will not parse&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;An apostrophe in the message emits &lt;tt&gt;\&apos;&lt;/tt&gt;, which is not a YAML escape:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;preformatted panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;preformattedContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;error: &quot;Health\ hasn\&apos;t\ recovered&quot;
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Any conformant parser rejects the &lt;b&gt;whole document&lt;/b&gt;, not just that scalar:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;preformatted panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;preformattedContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;yaml.scanner.ScannerError: while scanning a double-quoted scalar
  found unknown escape character &quot;&apos;&quot;
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;So the run reports nothing at all. Note this is reachable only from a subtest that &lt;b&gt;failed&lt;/b&gt; &#8212; the &lt;tt&gt;error&lt;/tt&gt; field is empty for a pass &#8212; so it fires exactly when the report is wanted. &quot;Health hasn&apos;t recovered&quot; is a real message from &lt;tt&gt;wait_recovery_complete()&lt;/tt&gt;; &quot;can&apos;t open ...&quot; messages hit it too.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;&lt;a name=&quot;Symptom2%3Athemessageisrecordedwrong&quot;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Symptom 2: the message is recorded wrong&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A message holding a newline or tab gets bash ANSI-C quoting instead. That &lt;b&gt;parses&lt;/b&gt;, and the recorded value silently keeps the literal wrapper:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;preformatted panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;preformattedContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;in:     &quot;line one\nline two\ttabbed&quot;
out:    error: &quot;$&apos;line one\nline two\ttabbed&apos;&quot;
parsed: $&apos;line one\nline two\ttabbed&apos;
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;&lt;a name=&quot;Fix&quot;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Fix&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Write a &lt;b&gt;single&lt;/b&gt;-quoted YAML scalar. It takes no backslash escapes at all, so &lt;tt&gt;&apos;&apos;&lt;/tt&gt; is the only sequence needing care and the message cannot introduce syntax. Fold newlines and tabs to spaces first, to keep the scalar on one line.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Messages containing no such character are unaffected in value: &lt;tt&gt;%q&lt;/tt&gt; wrote &lt;tt&gt;&quot;Out\ of\ memory&quot;&lt;/tt&gt;, which decoded to the same string the single-quoted form now carries directly.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;&lt;a name=&quot;Verification&quot;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Verification&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Driving the real function over nine messages and parsing each result: the old format broke or corrupted &lt;b&gt;5 of 9&lt;/b&gt;; the new format is correct on &lt;b&gt;9 of 9&lt;/b&gt; &#8212; apostrophes, doubled apostrophes, embedded double quotes, &lt;tt&gt;$ &amp;amp; % ; &amp;lt; &amp;gt;&lt;/tt&gt;, globs, brackets, trailing backslash, and multiline.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;&lt;a name=&quot;Impact&quot;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Impact&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Any consumer of &lt;tt&gt;results.yml&lt;/tt&gt; &#8212; Maloo, &lt;tt&gt;ltvm test&lt;/tt&gt;, or a hand-rolled parser &#8212; loses a whole run&apos;s results whenever a failure message contains an apostrophe. A raw control character in a message (for example an escape sequence) is still not handled and is out of scope here.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
